The Wizard sub-clan of the Angelika clan was in an uproar. Ever since
Angelika the Valkyrie became a demigoddess, members of the Wizard
sub-clan had tried to match her feat. Without success. They had so far
kept their lack of success a quiet secret within the Wizard sub-clan,
but they knew they had to succeed soon or the rest of the Angelika
clan would discover their failure and then there would be no stopping
the demeaning jokes (they had been bragging about their impending
success prematurely). So, a plenary session of the sub-clan had been
called to discuss the matter.

"Just give me a Wand of Wishing for starters and I'll show 'em!" said
Angelika.

"Can't do that. It's against The Rules," explained (another) Angelika.

"The Rules!? Screw The Rules! We need an Ascension, quickly! We can't
be fussy about things. Listen," said Angelika, lowering her voice,
"I've heard about something called Wiz Mode. We could --"

"Blasphemy!! You're suggesting we demean the Sacred Rules with
trickery, subvert Lord RNG! How dare you!" shouted (a different)
Angelika. "You don't deserve to be in the Wizard sub-clan. Maybe you
should join something more suitable -- like the Barbarians."

"Why YOU LITTLE --" and Angelika swung her quarterstaff at Angelika,
sending her across the room! The other Angelikas leapt to their feet
and a general melee began. (Not exactly the behavior one would expect
from a group of super-intelligent Wizards. But, then again, they were
all chaotic elves.) But one figure did not join in. Off in a corner
Angelika, the chaotic elven Wizard, sat shaking her head in disbelief
at her fellow Angelikas. Finally, she had had enough. "STOP THIS!!
STOP! LISTEN TO ME!", she shouted, pounding her quarterstaff on the
floor. After a few minutes, the others began to quiet down and give
Angelika their attention.

"We have to approach this logically," said Angelika, "We know from
divination what happened to the other Angelikas. Most of them starved
to death, and the others were too weak to survive for long. So, if we
fix those two problems nothing can stop us!"

"OK, Angelika Super-Genius, why don't you tell the rest of us how YOU
are going to ascend," said a rather disheveled Angelika.

Angelika thought, "ME!? Ascend? Maybe I should have kept my mouth
shut." Aloud, she said, "Well, first off, we have to fix the food
issue. We can't start with food, but we CAN start with a Ring of Slow
Digestion. Angelika, you have one, right? Cough it up!"

"But ... I need it," said a chubby Angelika.

"You have enough excess flab to get through ten Ascensions. Now, give
it to me!"

Angelika glowered, but she handed the ring over.

"Good. Now. The next problem is puniness. We just can't survive long
enough if we get surrounded or weak. We need help."

Another Angelika spoke up. "But, we get help," she said, holding up
Toonces, one of a litter of several thousand kittens named Toonces.

Angelika sighed and rubbed her temples. "We need a little MORE help
than that. You've heard my cousin Angelika the Valkyrie's story,
haven't you? The moron repeats it whenever anyone looks at her, so you
must have. She may have survived without a pet, but we Wizards need
one. A BIG one! There are Things down there in the Dungeon. Things
with claws!.

"Toonces has claws, don't you, sweetie?" said Angelika, giving the
kitten a peck on its forehead.

"Things with BIG claws! And Fangs!"

"Toonces has f--"

"Shut up. Listen. We have to get a big, MEAN pet right away. And we
know what that means," said Angelika, turning to eye the Angelika who
was gushing over Toonces. "Come on. Fork it over!" The other Angelika
looked at Angelika nervously: "What do you mean?"

"I mean, give me the Wand of Polymorph, you fool!"

"Um ... It's all used up."

"Oh. You used it already? Well, okay, what did you make? A dragon? A
titan? An archon, maybe? Any of those would be great at the start."

"Well, ah, I, ah ... I made more kittens."

Angelika just stood and stared for moment. "You. Made. More. Kittens?
ARE YOU INSANE!? We're drowning in the damn things!"

"But, I like kittens."

Stifling the impulse to strangle her clan-mate, Angelika addressed the
general audience: "Look, people, I need some good starting
equipment. What can you give me?"

It turns out the Angelikas had very little to offer -- or, at least,
very little they were willing to offer.

"A wand of cancellation? A spellbook of healing? A few potions? Is
that it?" Angelika sighed. "Well, at least I have my own magic
marker."

Angelika put her possessions into her kit, and turned to the
others. "Okay, I guess I've elected myself to be next. Try not to poke
each other's eyes out while I'm away." With that she grabbed (a)
Toonces and headed off to the Dungeon entrance.

"What the hell am I doing," she thought, "Me and my big mouth. 'We
have to approach this logically.' Yeah, right. 'If we fix those two
problems nothing can stop us.' Phooey! The Dungeons of Doom never go
the way you expect. It's like trying to plan a tornado." She trudged
on, and finally reached a large cave opening with a sign, "Last Rest
Rooms for Fifty Levels!" Angelika took care of some personal business,
and then headed in. "Okay, Toonces, let's go ..."

[Editor's Note: It occurred to me during the writing of this preamble
that some people might think Angelika acquired her starting equipment
by cheating. This is not so. The preamble is Based on a True Story,
and like most movies Based on a True Story is almost entirely made
up. The sub-clan really was in an uproar and things did get nasty at
times, but the dramatic details were invented purely for your
entertainment. Angelika's Ascension was 100% organic with no unnatural
additives. All her equipment was provided by Lord RNG. We now return
you to our regularly scheduled YAAP.]

The Ascension of Angelika: A Take of Determination and Mis-Steps

Angelika was determined to not blunder her way through an ascension
like her idiot cousin the Valkyrie, but in the back of her mind she
knew that the Dungeons of Doom and Lord Rng were not to be trifled
with.

Things start out quietly. She finds a lawful altar on 2, but fails to
convert it. She doesn't yet know that, except for the altar in Mine
Town and the ones in Gehemmon, this will be it for altars. 

And then Angelika has some good luck: she finds a Wand of Polymorph on
level 3, and decides her kitten Toonces could use a makeover. She zaps
Toonces and admires her new guardian naga pet. "Okay, let's give this a
try."  The advantages of a guardian naga quickly become evident, as he
uses his ability to paralyze people to kill Aksaray, the keeper of an
armor shop on DL4. Unfortunately, the small shop contains nothing of
interest (to a Wizard, that is), but she does get a key, lots of gold,
and a wand of striking from the late shopkeeper. She finds the Mine
Entrance, and after exploring the rest of DL4 (and getting telepathy
from a floating eye), decides to show her new pet the famous Mines.

During the trek to Mine Town, Tooonces performs superbly, easily
eliminating whatever foe made the mistake of confronting them. She
finds a blindfold on level 2 of the mines, to complement her
telepathy. 

Upon reaching Mine Town Toonces "goes to town" (so to speak) and
quickly slaughters a number of shopkeepers. Angelika was a little
shocked to discover that Toonces's first victim was the venerable
Izchak, but, well, she didn't TELL Toonces to do it. She was busy
fighting off some random monsters during Toonces's little spree. In
fact, she had been hoping to price a lamp she had found, as well as
two lamps in his store. "Sorry, Izchak," she thinks, "but Lord Rgn had
it in for you today I guess."

Toonces is on a rampage, killing whatever enters the lighting
shop. Angelika doesn't want Toonces kill the priest, since she
wants to buy protection. So, after Toonces kills the watch captain in
the lighting store, she locks him inside. The altar turns out to be
neutral, but she pays for some protection and gets 2 points worth.

Angelika retrieves Toonces and leads him around to the other
shopkeepers so she can "inherit" the belongings of the
dear-departed. Using the gold, she buys more protection and gets her
naked AC down to 5. She then gives Toonces free reign and lets him run
around killing everything in sight (except for the still useful
priest).

So, Angelika finds herself with a bunch of now deserted stores:
-- Sperc's hardware (R.I.P.) 
-- Lighting store (R.I.P. Sorry, Izchak!)
-- Bodeyri's general store (R.I.P.)
-- Karankobar's deli (R.I.P.)

She makes Izchak's shop her office, and goes around collecting useful
items to either use or stash there. She finds a pair of +2 padded gloves
that bring her AC to -3. Studded leather armor brings that down to -6
(spell failure = 3%). 

Angelika decides she really wants an altar. Not wanting to anger the
still useful priest, she heads back to 2 and fails in two
more attempts to convert. However, the fourth attempt succeeds. She
uses a key she got from a late shopkeeper to open a box on DL1 and
finds a spellbook of haste self. She also gets poison resistance from
a killer bee on DL3.

Time for some holy water. While diluting potions of fruit juice in
Mine Town, a fountain breaks and makes a flood. This will be useful
later for diluting, after she get an AoMB. She prays for HW on 2, and
then blesses her magic marker (starting equipment) and writes two
blessed IDs; the second gives a full inventory ID. She enchants her
CoMR to +2, blessed. She goes back to Mine Town to find that a rock
mole has ruined most of the rooms, but she does find one intact room
and establishes a stash there.  She does some sacrificing on 2, and
stashes more things in the chest on 3, including some seed holy water.

The sacrifice messages show it's safe to pray. Angelika decides to
save that in case she gets in trouble later. She considers her
options: Mine's End or Sokoban? Her AC is -8 and Toonces is being
good, but she doesn't feel up to major combat yet, so she decides on a
third option: find the vault on DL5 first (she'd heard the tread of
guards) and see if she gets enough $ to buy more protection.

Angelika alters her plan a bit when she finds a liquor store on
DL5. She waits discreetly just outside while Toonces has a few words
with the shopkeeper, and she then has plenty of holy water fodder. So,
she decides dipping in fountains for an early wish would be a good
idea. She gathers up the useless potions, leaves a stash in the store
to get unstressed, and then heads for DL3 which has 3 fountains. 

The first dip produces a hostile water demon, but he's no match for
Toonces and Angelika. Later on she gets another hostile demon who
summons a succubus; they are disposed of readily. All the fountains
dry up, so she heads to DL4 which has another fountain, and gets
another hostile demon. After that fountain dries up, she heads to DL5
and dries up the fountain there with more dipping. 

"All that dipping, and no wish. Blah," she thinks. But she does have
lots of water, so she heads back to DL3 to get her seed holy water and
makes plenty of HW. She blesses potions of see invisible,
invisibility, and gain ability (2 of these). Having acquired permanent
invisibility and see invisible, she leaves her excess HW in the chest
on 3 and then heads to Mine Town (locking Toonces up to prevent any
"accidents" with the priest), and buys protection to get her AC to
-9. 

Angelika decides to head for Sokoban. On the way she loots the vault
on 5. A guard shows up but she knows the answer to the question.

She finds a crystal ball on DL6, but picking it up makes her stressed
so she leaves it for later. 6 is also the Oracle level. Angelika
smashes the statues and finds nothing. Zip. Nada. In fact, she has
found nothng in any other statues she's encountered, and she wonders
if she's doing something wrong, but a passing Rgrn daemon explains
Lord Rgn is just being cranky. On DL7 she gets a unicorn horn when
Toonces kills a black unicorn. There's also a throne room there. And
Sokoban. Angelika establishes another stash in a chest in the throne
room. She sits on the throne and gets some hit points.

Angelika does Sokoban which is mostly uneventful, though Toonces does
fall through a hole and she has to scurry down a level to retrieve
him. On one of the Sokoban levels, Toonces nearly killed Angelika with
laughter over the following antics:

Toonces bites the floating eye.
The floating eye is frozen by Toonces.
Toonces is frozen by the floating eye's gaze!

And there they stood, staring each other down. The eye recovered first
and Angelika destroyed it with a force bolt. 

The monsters in the Sokoban zoo fell to the Angelika-Toonces tag team
and Angelika acquired a BoH. 

Angelika does another round of BUC at the altar on 2 and IDs some
things. She has rings of polymorph control and teleport control. She
puts more stuff in her stash on DL3 and heads to Mine Town to prepare
for Mine's End. She buys another point of protection and then heads
for Mine's End with Toonces in tow (after having him deal with an
annoying infestation of peaceful gremlins).

The first level down, she finds a leash and Toonces is very
accommodating. Angelika decides she likes guardian naga pets: They
paralyze opponents, don't eat her food or pick up things she wants,
and they take well to leashes. Little did she know that her
relationship with her pet was headed for tragedy.

At Mine's End Toonces steps on a teleport trap and
disappears. Angelika tries to find him with telepathy, but doesn't see
him. Could he have gone to another level? She wants to find him before
he is no longer tame.  She searches all the mine levels, and then all
the main dungeon levels from 1 to 10 with no luck. She finally finds
him back in Mine'e End! She realizes she didn't recognize him from
telepathy because his color had changed from a nice neon green to dark
green. He is no longer Angelika's pet, just peaceful. Another Rgrn
Daemon said this was likely a side effect of his not eating, which
makes him more likely to become peaceful or feral. She pledges to
return for Toonces someday when she has the means to tame him.

She returns to Mine Town after blessing the luckstone and discovers
that Tringanoe, a deli owner, is still alive! Apparently he'd been
hiding behind his counter during Toonces's rampage. Angelika is
actually glad for the company, sharing a couple of potions of Booze
with him as she tells him how much she misses her pet. Tringanoe
listens but is more interested in Angelika's money.

She does some more dipping in Mine Town and gets water mocassins for
her trouble. She goes back to the altar on 2 and BUCs things. A white
unicorn shows up and thoughtfully dies right on the altar. How
convenient! 

Angelika discovers she has a wand of enlightenment and zapping this
reveals:

 You are piously aligned.
 You are sleep resistant.
 You are poison resistant.
 You are magic-protected.
 You see invisible.
 You are telepathic.
 You have infravision.
 You are invisible to others.
 You have slower digestion.
 You are protected.
 You are fast.
 You have fixed abilities.  <== ring of sustain ability
 You are very lucky.
 You have extra luck.
 Good luck does not time out for you.
 You can safely pray.

She knows she has a few problems. She only has sleep and poison
resistance (she's tried to get others without success). Fair armor
(-9). No pet. No Magicbane.

She writes a blessed scroll of taming and heads back for Toonces, but the
scroll of taming fails to work! "Must be his inherent magic resistance.
I'll try again later," she thinks and continues her adventures.

She finds the Big Room on level 10, which has a convenient cockatrice
near the stairs. She kills it and soon the Big Room has a splendid
display of realistic representations of dungeon denizens. 

She finds the entrance to Fort Ludios on 11. She makes another stash
in a chest on 8 and then tackles the Fort.

In Ludios she has some trouble with a mountain nymph, but she gets her
stuff back. She eats a leprechaun corpse to get teleportitis and
replaces her ring of sustain ability with her ring of TC. Ludios is a
big and difficult battle. She decides she needs to lower her AC before
completing Ludios. A better weapon would be nice, but Anhur has so far
given her nothing from sacrificing and she hasn't found anything
really good. She gets enough gold to go chat with the priest in Mine
Town again and get her naked AC down to 2. She then scours the Mines
for better armor and weapons. She finds better armor and gets her AC
down to -12.

Angelika is not too pleased with the results of her scavenging, so she
decides to change strategies. She returns to Ludios and swaps her ring
of teleport control for a ring of conflict. This stategy works well
until a black dragon destroys her CoMR and studded leather armor,
leaving her AC at -5. And no MR. She makes a strategic retreat (i.e.,
runs away) and swears to return to Ludios later to teach that dragon a
lesson. 

Angelika is feeling a little discouraged, but she is determined not to
let down the Wizard sub-clan, so she sets out to repair the
damage. She really wants Magicbane, so she returns to the altar on 2
to do more sacrificing. Fickle Anhur takes pity on her and gives her
Magicbane immediately. She gets intrinsic TC from a tengu corpse, and
then Anhur gives her Stormbringer. One of her sacrificial lambs drops
a wand of create monster, and she settles down for a real sacfest but
all she gets is a bunch of four leaf clovers. 

She looks for a cloak and finds a cloak of displacement. Nice, but the
magic cancellation is only 2. 

She decides to dungeon dive and leave Ludios alone for a while. On the
Oracle level she dilutes some potions and gets a grateful water demon
for a change. SDSM, please. All of a sudden her AC is -17. On 12 she
finds a spellbook of identify in a chest, and discovers she has a
scroll of genocide. She blesses it and keeps it for later. Although
this is a reasonable (some would say preferable) strategy, she would
live to regret the decision not to just use it right away.

Her dungeon diving does not grant her any boons. She finds the quest
portal on 13, but she is only XL 12. She finds a graveyard on 14, and
hopes to gain a couple of levels from wraith corpses. Instead, she gets
drained a level by a wraith who then leaves a corpse so she can get
back to where she was (minus a few thousand XP). She deals with an
anthole on 15.

Angelika is bored. And she still has a grudge against that black
dragon in Ludios. She has reflection now, and MR from
Magicbane. Although she feels underpowered as far as attacks go, she
feels her armor and wits will get her through Ludios. So, back she
goes, and the black dragons are foiled by her SDSM. She examines the
armor lying around, selects some choice pieces and gets her AC down to
-20. She is happy about her AC, but she's not sure what kind of
fashion statement she's making. A blessed +2 dented pot? (It was just
lying there.) Well, she can leave out that little detail when she
recounts her adventures at the next clan re-union. 

She doesn't have levitation so she decides to leave Ludios again. She
could get across the moat using the Scrolls of Earth from Sokoban, but
decides to save those for now. Before she leaves, she gets some
revenge by eating a black dragon corpse and getting disintegration
resistance.

Angelika sighs (thinking of the loot in Ludios she is leaving behind
once again) and starts to dungeon dive again. She finds a SoEA on 17,
blesses it, and gets her SDSM to +5. AC is now -23. 

She finds a graveyard on 19, and wants to use some wraith corpses to
get some levels. But she is still satiated and needs to wait until she
can safely eat. She removes her RoSD (she has lots of food now, so
she's in no danger), and makes her way to the altar on 2 to try to get
something useful from Anhur while waiting to get hungry. On her way up
she trades her lovely blessed +2 dented pot for a more debonair
blessed +2 orcish helm. (The orcish race actually has a surprising
sense of style, in a primitive I-like-to-chop-your-body-parts-off kind
of way.) She also swaps her cloak of displacement for a plain elven
cloak for the extra magic cancellation. And she finds blessed +3 iron
shoes that get her AC to -24, with a slight increase in spell
failure. She's feeling like this trip upstairs has been well worth it.

Arriving on 2, she encounters an Aleax who drops a shield of
reflection. Turning to the altar to begin her sacrificing, Angelika
thinks, "I actually WANT to be crowned. I lack a lot of
useful resistances (fire, cold, and shock) in spite of my efforts to
acquire them. I think I can live with the increase in prayer timeout,
since I have plenty of WoCM to get back into Anhur's good graces. AND --
I want that spellbook of Finger of Death. That will be VERY nice!"

So she begins. Whenever it's safe, she prays. She gets 5 HP. She gets
her armor blessed. On her third prayer she gets crowned -- but no
object appears at her feet!! "Hey!!! Where's my spellbook?!" Her sword
Stormbringer glowed, but that's it. After spending some time fuming at
her fickle god, she decides to consult her Spellbook of Spoiling and
discovers she only gets the spellbook IF she is not wielding
Stormbringer when she is crowned. "#$&@*!" she thinks. Well, at least
she got her resistances:

You are the Glory of Arioch.
You are piously aligned.
You are fire resistant.
You are cold resistant.
You are sleep resistant.
You are disintegration-resistant.
You are shock resistant.
You are poison resistant.
You are level-drain resistant.
You see invisible.
You are telepathic.
You have infravision.
You are invisible to others.
You are stealthy.
You can teleport.
You have teleport control.
You can survive without air. <== amulet of magic breathing
You are protected.
You are fast.
You have reflection.
You have fixed abilities.
You are extremely lucky.
You have extra luck.
Good luck does not time out for you.
You can not safely pray.

On her way down to chat with the priest in Mine Town, Angelika
befriends a dog named Choochie whom she turns into a master lich
(after being a floating eye for a bit). Choochie becomes
invisible. She buys another point of protection from the priest. AC is
now -25.

Choochie follows her down to the graveyard. She likes the fact that
he's invisible and teleports close to her if they get
separated. However, this means she can't genocide L without
polymorphing Choochie first. 

Angelika approached the graveyard battle with high hopes of gaining
some levels from wraith corpses. However, the wraiths were not
cooperative about leaving corpses. Finally, she gets a wraith corpse,
but a vampire steps over it, makes a hole with a wand of digging and
drops through. She tries to get the corpse anyway hoping she will
escape the hole, but she and Choochie both drop through to level
20. On 20, the V pulls the same trick, and Choochie goes after
him. Angelika goes down and leads Choochie back up to the graveyard to
finish that battle. It turns out the wraith corpse that was on the
hole is the only one created!

Angelika is rather pissed at the vampire who ruined her chance to gain
a level, so she and Choochie go after him. They fight him on 21 and
22, and the V keeps pulling the same trick, falling through to 23. And
then 24, where he is finally vanquished. 

She gets 20K from a leprechaun hall on 23, so she decides to go back to
Mine Town to buy protection. She gets one point. AC -26. 

She goes back up to 2 to do more sacrificing. On 4 she gets a wraith
corpse -- which turns out to be rotten even though it was eaten
immediately. She finds a ring of searching. Yawn. On 2 she gets Fire
Brand from Anhur. 

Angelika decides to go back to Ludios and use one scroll of earth from
Sokoban to fill the moat so she can get across and finally loot the
treasure rooms. She puts a lot of stuff into a box on 11 (where the
Ludios portal is) to get unburdened. She reads a scroll of earth,
finds the secret door and starts the battle. She's embarrassed that
she's fighting like her cousin Angelika (though she is having fun),
but her attack spell repertoire is still very limited. She throws a
few force bolts in for good form. She wears her blindfold so she'll be
warned of any ; in the moat. She fills the moat around the door, kills
everything in sight (with minimal help from Choochie) and starts
looking for stuff. She finds some spellbooks, but the only unknown one
turns out to be detect treasure. She finds a stethoscope and uses it
to examine Choochie:

Status of Choochie (chaotic):  Level 36  HP 281(281)  AC -12, tame, fast,
invisible.

Not bad. 

She lets Choochie step on (most of) the land mines in the treasure
room. She nets 45K. (The throne just vanishes.) Time for more
protection. Back to Mine Town and she gets one more point. Naked AC is
-1.

Angelika still wants rings of levitation and free action, so she
decides to kick some sinks. The sink on 3 gives her puddings -- and a
ring! Stealth. Sigh. She also gets a dishwasher, who is not
useful. She goes back to Mine town to try a sink there, and puts
Choochie up one level so he won't kill the priest. From that sink
she gets puddings and another ring of PC. When she returns to the
previous level, she finds that Choochie is peaceful. That makes two
pets to retrieve later. 

Somwhere she finds a spellbook of levitation. That's helpful, but she
would rather have a ring so she can control exactly when the levitation
ends. 

On the way to Mine's End to dip into the fountains, she forgets to
switch between Fire brand and Magicbane and steps on a poly
trap. Presto! Instant silver dragon. And no more elven cloak. She
decides she might as well lay some eggs. She lays three, and
soon Moe, Larry, and Curly are born. She returns to elven form and
still has her SDSM, but no cloak. She visits Toonces at Mine's End:

Status of Toonces (lawful):  Level 18  HP 144(144)  AC 0, peaceful.

Angelika achieves XL 14 and then drinks a bPoGL to get to 15. Time
to go on the quest. She brings Curly and Larry with her (herding three
pets without a magic whistle is just too hard). 

Curly is killed on the way up by some explosion. She slips a leash
around Larry and continues. Larry's info:

Status of Larry (neutral):  Level 11  HP 58(58)  AC 2, tame.

Angelika gets a spare cloak of displacement from her stash on 3, but this
only has MC = 2. She hasn't seen another elven cloak, probably because
they are all worn by peaceful elves she has not attacked. "Hmmm. Perhaps
Larry can help here," she thinks. On level 7, he does, removing an an
inconsequential invisible Woodland Elf. Angelika swaps the elven cloak for the
CoD which goes into the BoH.

She arrives at the Lonely Tower, Larry in tow. They fight off the
multitude (including the second Nazgul she's encountered -- she will
wind up killing all nine of them!), and she speaks with Neferet the
Green. She finds a spellbook of magic missile in Neferet's chest! This
is a welcome addition to her repertoire.

Larry is killed by a Xorn! "I'm having great luck with pets," she
thinks. On her way to the Dark One, she finds gauntlets of dexterity,
and another scroll of genocide. And she also steps into some water by
accident. This has repercussions later. On the Dark One's level, she is
briefly excited when she finds another ring. Hunger. Groan. 

Before the battle:

Status of the Dark One (chaotic):  Level 15  HP 64(64)  AC 0,
meditating.

Angelika battles him all the way up to the Lonely Tower, and he dies in
the Tower itself. She collects the Bell and the Eye and continues her
dungeon diving. 

On 26 she finds the Medusa level. But she still lacks a ring of
levitation. Or free action. Well, okay, there are more sinks to
kick. The sink on 7 gives her an enormously useless ring of poison
resistance, and the one on 17 gives her a ring of warning. Arrgh!

So, she'll have to use the levitation spell to tackle Medusa, much as
she doesn't like it.

Angelika decends to the Medusa level, but when she enters the level a
titan starts a summoning storm. Angelika starts doing the fight a bit,
go upstairs to heal, go down and fight again trick. She's having fun
doing this. She should have remembered that "it's fun until someone
loses an eye." In this case, it's fun until a xan scratches her leg
and she becomes stressed and can't get up the stairs. This began the
scariest part of her adventure. So many things were hitting her, she
couldn't get to a place where she could dig (and her wand of digging
was in her BoH anyway, and taking a turn to get it out could have been
fatal), and she couldn't go upstairs to rest. She had taken out two
blessed scrolls of genocide in her main inventory during one of her
rest stops upstairs, figuring they were an adequate emergency
measure. Right now feels a lot like an emergency, so she tries
genociding H to get rid of the titan. Her first attempt is a near
disaster: some monster confuses her just before she reads the
scroll. Luckily, she realizes that her perception is impaired and
chooses to genocide nothing. She cures the confusion and then reads
the second scroll, only to find she can't genocide titans. Her HP get
down to 9 at one point and she prays to Anhur who heals her. Finally,
her leg heals and she goes up the stairs, breathing a deep sigh of
relief.

Angelika needs a strategy. She wants to go down to the next level. She
should probably just dig down, but she needs to be able to get to a
square where she can dig (not standing on the upstairs). And she is
royally PO'ed at the titan. She knows she's playing like her cousin
the Valkyrie, but she's MAD! She decides to just FIGHT!

So, back down she goes and a master mind flayer eats her brain. INT
goes to 17, but her unihorn fixes that. Finally, she gets the titan
with magic missile, and puts on a ring of conflict, which clears
things out. Surveying the carnage around her, she has to admit that
bashing things has its merits, though she knows she was daring Lord
Rgn to end her ascension attempt. Well, she did use SOME magic during
the battle. 

Angelika falls through a hole under some debris, and uses magic
mapping to find the upstairs. And comes up right next to
Medusa. Oops. Luckily, Medusa must have been facing away. Blindfold,
apply mirror, the end. However, she can't get back across the
water. The boots of levitation from Perseus are cursed, and she can't
remember the levitation spell. The spellbook seems to have been turned
to blank paper (the result of her mis-step into the water during the
quest). She has used the Holy Water that she had with her so she can't
uncurse the boots.

So, she goes down with a wand of digging. The Castle is on 26. She
can't get the tune on her bugle, so she destroys the drawbridge with a
wand of striking, and uses Magic Missile to kill monsters. A pair of
titans start summoning storms, and out comes the ring of conflict. She
uses the second scroll of earth from Sokoban and pushes boulders into
the moat. She engages in another major battle in the courtyard.

In the throne room, she finds spellbooks of Magic Missile, turn
undead, and clairvoyance in the chest behind the throne. The WoW is
0:1. After the de rigeur 2 blessed scrolls of charging, Angelika
considers her options. She wants both a ring of levitation and a ring
of free action, but that's two wishes and there's plenty else she
wants. Then she has an idea: Try polypiling the rings she has
first. She does this and gets two rings of lev from polypiling, one
cursed and one uncursed. This frees up one wish.

Angelika charges the wand and does her remaining wishes: blessed ring
of free action, blessed fixed +2 helm of brilliance, blessed magic
marker. The MM is 0:48, which gives her 3 bSoEA. She uses the second
scroll of charging and gets the MM up to 50. She decides to use the
last wish now for blessed fixed +2 boots of speed, a nice permanent
battle advantage. Writing more scrolls, she gets everything proofed
and her AC is now -31.

The throne gives her a shock and vanishes.

She goes back up to 2 for more sacrificing and praying, hoping she
will get the spellbook of finger of death she craves. She gets
intrinsic stealth. Nice, but not what she wanted. 

Angelika moves her main stash to 20 to prepare for the assault on the
Valley of the Dead and Gehennom, and then drops down through a castle
trapdoor to the VoD. She's still hoping for some wraith corpses. She's
XL 17, but is aiming for 30 for the HP, Pw, and spell ability slots. 

She only gets one wraith corpse in the VoD, to get to XL 18. There's a
moment of excitement when she finds a spellbook. Could it be?!
No. Jumping. Blah. She does find a Hawaiian shirt. (On an orc. See,
they do have a sense of style, sort of). 

On the first level of Gehennom, Angelika meets a nurse, and gives into
temptation. She finds she rather likes it. A lot, actually. She also
meets an incubus, who teaches her some things they don't mention in
Hogwart's. She gets to XL 19 and decides she likes this a lot, even
though she is, um, "relaxing" in the very pit of hell. She gets the
nurse and incubus together and tries a threesome, but the incubus
seems to have taken up S&M and just bashes her, so she takes him out
with magic missile. Meanwhile, a second nurse appears and Angelika
convinces the two to try another threesome. After a while, a third
nurse appears!

[Editor's note: What followed was somewhat sordid and we shall
discreetly avert our eyes as our heroine indulges her baser
instincts.]

Feeling refreshed, Angelika decides to spend some time making HW, UHW
(she had found a potion of UHW) and praying. She prays and an object
appears! A spellbook! Confuse Monster. Foo. She prays again and gets
some HP, bringing hr to 152. 

Angelika starts to think about those nurses again and the incubus: "The
nurses are still down there on 28, and I don't really have anything
better to do, do I? I mean there's that Amulet business, but
getting HP will help that, right?, so I really OUGHT to go, um,
recreate again."

Back down to 28 she goes, picking up a scroll of genocide on the way
(goodbye, L). She gets a few more HP before the nurses disappear. 156
total now.

She meets and destroys Asmodeus on 29, and gets some boring wands. She
falls through a trapdoor on 30, down to 32 where she finds Baalzebub,
whom she leaves alone for now. She goes up to 31 which is Juiblex,
who is easily destroyed using the standard wand of digging trick. She
finds a blessed crystal ball in his swamp, so she now has two. She
establishes a stash in the temple in the VoD with both of the crystal
balls for use on the Planes.

On 32 she finds a magic marker(0:80). Choices: Try writing finger of
death, write EA and EW, write genocide. Decision: Bless the MM, write
charging, write three EA, charge MM and see if it goes above 70. If
so, write FoD, else write EA, EW, Genocide. She blesses the MM, writes
blessed charging, writes bSoEA and gets her speed boots and shirt to
+5 each (saving the cloak to last in case she finds a cloak of
protection -- having intrinsic stealth, she decides to go for better
AC with the same MC). There are 35 charges left when she reads the
scroll of charging, and the MM has 75 after. Excited, she tries to
write FoD and succeeds! And 0% failure! The MM has 13 charges left,
enough for gold detection, magic mapping, earth, and a few other
possibly useful scrolls, so she keeps it for later. AC is -38. A few
minutes later -- she finds a cloak of protecion! She heads back to 27
to get a scroll of destroy armor to fireproof her new cloak. This gets
her AC to -40.

Angelika is feeling quite pleased with herself, so she takes on
Baalzebub and disposes of him in Juiblex's swamp. 

On 33 she finds a spellbook of charm monster. She heads back to the
mines to get Toonces and Moe (Choochie, of course, is gone because of
her blessed genocide of L.) 

On the way up she meets a very attactive incubus on 27, the VoD, which
happens to be no teleport, and they're in a room she can lock! Rubbing
her hands with glee, Angelika ...

[Editor's note: Once again we shall avert our eyes. Suffice it to say
that Angelika acquires some Pw points and levels 22, 23, 24, 25, 26,
and 27 from this very cooperative incubus. The cooperation may have
been encouraged by Angelika's imprisonment of the poor demon and her
barely veiled threats to practice her new FoD spell on any
uncooperative creatures she happens upon. Minor intrusions from a
troll and earth elementals allow her to demonstrate her point to the
hapless incubus.]

Tossing aside the worn out incubus like a rubber doll, Angelika dons a
blindfold to determine what has appeared in the VoD during her little
vacation. What's this?! Two NURSES!! Woo-Hoo!!! Tearing off her
clothing, Angelika ...

[Editor's note: Okay. Again. Not to sound prudish, but this is getting
to be a bit much. Anyway, after the orgy, Angelika is XL 27, HP 182,
and Pw 504. She takes time out from her debauchery to dispose of a
balrog and a master mind flayer. It seems the danger of it all
actually turns her on.]

Angelika heads back to the mines to retrieve her pets, feeling a bit
lonely when she passes through the level that had once housed
Choochie. In Mine Town she tries buying protection, but to no
avail. She takes the time to perform some alchemy and winds up with 30
blessed diluted potions of full healing. She reserves 5 and drinks the
rest. A pyrolisk wanders by while she is quaffing and destroys 6 of
the potions! Still, her HP are now 334.

She goes to Mine's End and tames Toonces and Moe:

Status of Toonces (lawful):  Level 18  HP 144(144)  AC 0, tame.

Status of Moe (neutral):  Level 11  HP 63(63)  AC 2, tame.

Angelika is overjoyed to have her pets back, but the joy is short
lived.  Moe gets turned into a cat on the way up to Mine Town. Okay,
she can turn him into something more useful later. But the real
problem happens on Medusa's level. Angelika wanders out into the
middle of the level to check out some stuff on one of the islands. On
the way back to where she left her pets, a voice tells her that
Toonces has drowned!  She feels guilty about this, although she can't
think why she had any responsibility for this. Toonces wasn't on a
leash, and in fact was nowhere near Angelika when he apparently
decided to end it all. Anhur is angry and Angelika can't seem to
appease him with the WoCM at the altar on 2.

She goes back down to Medusa, and leaves little Moe on an island
there. "I'm just poison to pets, honey, so you'll be better off by
yourself," she says to him. "Besides you're a useless pain in the
butt," she says to herself.

Angelika heads down to the VoD. She's feeling a bit down over her
pets. She wishes she had a way to cheer herself up. Some kind of
distraction, maybe a -- Hello? What's that over there in a nice,
cramped little corner? A NURSE!! "Well, well," she says, "I believe
we'll start out with a little ..."

[Editor's note: Me, again. I give up. Obviously, there's no stopping
Angelika's appetites, so we'll just have to get used to periodic
interruptions to our narrative. At least this time the nurse seemed to
enjoy the danger of "doing it" in the pit of hell as much as
Angelika. She winds up getting 32 HP from this single nurse, bringing
her total to 366.]

"Tell your friends I'm always ready for a little party," she says to
the spent nurse. She continues down and befriends a new pet, Dudley
the blue dragon. 

On 35, an incubus shows up. "I hear you like to party," he says, and
Angelika ...

[Editor's note: She gets XL 28 and 29.]

After satiating herself, and not on food, Angelika notices that the
entrance to Vlad's Tower is also on 35. Dudley vanishes, probably
dead. "I really am poison," she thinks. This depresses her again, and
she decides she needs to make peace with her god. So, she begins the
trek back up to 2 to sacrifice and pray. On the way, she runs into
another nurse in Juiblex's swamp, and she ...

[Editor's note: 5 more HP, total 377. But here we must relate an
incident that occurred during her daliance. In a fit of passion,
Angelika falls into the water. She thought nothing of it at the time,
but this mis-step was to have dire consequences later.]

Continuing up, she gets XL 30 from a wraith on 29 (Asmodeus). On the
Castle level she finds ...

[Editor's note: Go ahead. Guess. Guess what she finds. Right. A
nurse. After more hot and sweaty action, she gets 17 HP and winds up
at 397 total.]

On 2, she finds that Anhur is still angry, but he is mollified by the
second sacrifice. The next few give her four leaf clovers. She prays
and gets a point of protection, bringing her AC to -41. She sacrifices
some more till she can pray safely. She saves the remaining charges in
the WoCM and goes to visit Vlad.

On the way to Vlad she tries FoD and is told her knowledge of the spell
is growing faint. "No problem, I'll just study it." She searches through
her BoH and discovers that she has a number of nice, blessed BLANK
spellbooks. Thinking back she realizes that her fall into the water in
Juiblex's swamp must have blanked that book and several others, including
magic mapping and magic missile, though luckily she has a spare of the
latter.

All of a sudden, Angelika is not feeling so confident. She wanted to
ascend like a real Wizard, Fingering anything that got in her way. She
hopes she can acquire another FoD spellbook. At least she's pumped up
her HP and Pw from her X-rated adventures. 

Angelika disposes of Vlad the Wimp and gets the candelabrum. She
continues down, and finds Orcus Town on 38. There is cockatrice on 36,
so she plans to get a c corpse for her confrontation with Orcus after
clearing out most of the level. However, during the numerous
skirmishes she has battling her way across the level, a captain
decides to read a SoCM -- and makes a cockatrice who conveniently
leaves a corpse. Within a few minutes, Orcus Town has a marvelous
collection of art. Orcus, unfortunately, uses two charges from his
wand before becoming a work of art himself, so his wand is only 0:2. 

Level 40 has the top of Rodney's Tower, and the bottom is on 44. 47
turns out to be the bottom of the dungeon. "That sign was wrong," she
thinks. While searching for the vibrating square, she encounters
Yeenoghu. She fights him a bit, but leaves him alone when he runs
upstairs. (She kills him later in a protracted but not very
interesting battle.) She has a great deal of trouble find the VS, but
she finally gets it and marks it with a couple of oranges (and
Elbereth).

Time to prepare for the end game. Angelika decides to polypile to get
either a magic marker or a spellbook of FoD. What she gets (of value)
is an oilskin sack ("Where were you when I needed you," she thinks)
and a spellbook of create monster. 

She does some more alchemy and gets her HP to 421.

Angelika decides to use her new create monster spell to do a lot of
praying on 2, to see if Anhur would please, please, please give her a
spellbook of FoD. First prayer: nothing. Second prayer: spellbook of
restore ability. Third: a spellbook of dig. Fourth: spellbook of
protection. Fifth: nothing. Sixth: nothing. Seventh: golden glow (5
HP). 

During all the monster conjuring that went into these prayers,
Angelika gets a wraith (good for 4 HP and 22 Pw), and another NURSE --
"Hey -- Wanna PART-TEEE??" said Angelika as she ...

[Editor's note: Sheesh. I mean, next to an altar? And doesn't she know
her sub-clan members are watching her through divination? This is all
just too sordid. Anyway, Angelika gets a whopping 48 HP from this
nurse, which she thinks must be some kind of record. And I might as
well save some time by telling you that she conjured three more
nurses, and got 1 HP, 4 HP, and 3 HP from them. Oh, and another wraith
for 4 HP and 20 Pw. All this debauchery is bound to lead to something
bad.]

Angelika examined herself in her looking glass. "Mmmmm. Very nice. 489
HP and 611 Pw. I'm more buff than my cousin now! I think I'll just
keep going." So, she does more monster conjuring, sacrificing,
praying. Her eighth prayer nets her a golden glow for 5 more HP. She
starts conjuring and sacrificing again to get to the point where she
can pray again, and lo and behold -- another nurse! Stripping quickly,
Angelika prepares to ravish the new arrival, when she realizes it's
really a doppelganger. Magic Missile takes care of it and she
sacrifices the corpse. She conjures again and the next monster is a
cockatrice, who leaves a corpse. Reaching down to get it so she can
put it on the altar ...

[Editor's note: I said something bad would come of this debauchery,
didn't I? Let this be a lesson to you all!]

... she picks up the the c corpse and immediately has the scariest
moment of her entire adventure. "You have made a fatal mistake!"
shouts a mysterious voice, and she realizes she will suffer a fate
worse than death -- she will become a work of art! But wait -- she is
still wearing her AoLS! It crumbles to dust, and she spends a few
moments recovering from the shock. "Maybe I should get dressed." She
does, and also dons her spare AoLS (from Vlad's place). 

Angelika continues her conjuring and praying, actually hoping she WON'T
see a nurse for a change. Ninth prayer: spellbook of drain life. She
gets another wraith corpse for 3 HP and 16 Pw. Tenth prayer: spellbook
of cure sickness. 

Angelika looks around. The area around the altar can only be described
as a massive junkyard, littered with heaps of objects  dropped by the
dozens of monsters she has conjured and destroyed. "If I don't ascend,
I could come back here and open a hell of a General Store." She
sacrifices some more to get a feeling of reconciliation, and then
heads back downstairs. 

She has various minor adventures on the way down. She encounters some
more nurses, but the old joy just isn't there and she gets no HP from
any of them. She does more alchemy and quaffs more potions, bringing
herself up to 556 HP and 635 Pw. 

Angelika finds a magic whistle, so she decides to try having pets
again. She makes friends with two white dragons, Frosty and Snowy, and
a black dragon named Fabio. They all drop down to the VoD, where Snowy
is killed by a captain. On level 32, she befriends a blue dragon named
Satchmo. 

Angelika enters Rodney's tower and deals with the inhabitants of the
first floor, befriending a yellow dragon Chicita in the process.

Angelika opens the door to the treasure zoo and starts spraying the
place with magic missiles. She kills a few peacefuls. "Collateral
damage," she thinks, in a suitably chaotic fashion.

At the top of the tower is an incubus, right next to the
ladder. Angelika immediately gets more HP and Pw from him, though he is
the agressor in this case. There's a Titan in one of the larger rooms
who starts a summoning storm. Luckily, one of the first monsters is a
cockatrice who leaves a corpse. She starts stoning things in front of
the titan, and after a while the titan makes the mistake of wandering
over to where she is. "What a great statue! I wonder if his name was
David?" Angelika takes care of the rest of the menagerie. In spite of
the rubber chicken, it is still quite a battle, and her HP get below
400 at one point. Someone had a WoD, and it still has 4 charges when
she gets it from the statue. Chicita has gotten killed during the
melee.

She finds a cursed scroll of charging that she blesses and saves for the
WoD. She WoDs the Wizard, but not before he summons some friends. On the
way out she steps on a magic trap and gets more things to kill. She's
acquired a bunch of healing potions from all this fighting, and is
contemplating more alchemy.

Fabio and Frosty are still tame when she finds them; Satchmo is just
peaceful. She leads them down to the VS to do the invocation. She
lights the candelabrum, rings the bell, and starts to read the book,
when Fabio starts to hit her. "Cut it out. I don't have the patience
for this." She starts reading the book again, and Fabio starts hitting
her again (even though inspection shows he is still tame), so she
kills him, and hears the sound of thunder. "I guess Anhur is angry
again. Well, does he want the blasted Amulet or not?" She finishes the
invocation and enters the Sanctum. The battle is long but
uneventful. She gets another WoD which is 0:7. Hurray! The high priest
gets the WoD treatment, and Angelika acquires the Amulet, naming it AS
SEEN ON TV.

Reminding herself to get her crystal balls from the stash in the VoD,
she starts the ascension of the dungeon. The mysterious force was
rather insistent: 43-->43, 43-->43, 39-->39, 37-->37, 35-->35,
34-->35, 35-->36, 36-->36, 36-->36, 36-->36, 36-->37, 34-->35,
35-->35, 33-->33, Rodney appears on 31 (Juiblex), 28--->28, Rodney
again on 27 (VoD). She gets the crystal balls. At the Castle she
pauses to do some alchemy and gets her HP to 672.

At the altar on 2, she conjures a Jabberwock which she sacrifices and
gets a four leaf clover. Her wand of enlightenment confirms that she
can safely pray. "I guess Anhur wasn't all that angry."

Rodney shows up on 1. Angelika yawns and WoDs him. She takes out a
crystal ball and heads to the Planes.

Earth is a simple matter. Rodney bites the dust again, and the crystal
ball (CB) shows that the portal is nearby.

Air is more difficult. The portal is further away, and the Air
Elementals get her HP down to a relatively feeble 233 before she
reaches it.

She takes some timeout on Fire to do some extra healing spells. Rodney
shows up and it takes three shots from a WoD to get him.

She shows up on Water with 401 HP and does some extra healing spells
to get to 571. She uses the CB twice to find the moving portal, and
makes her way to it, destroying the odd monster along the way.

On the Astral Plane she meets a guardian angel who wields
Demonbane. Using her blindfold, she takes the lay of the land: Famine
is middle, Pestilence is left, and death is right. She decides to go
to the center first. She fights an Angel of Moloch with Magicbane,
WoDs Famine, then uses teleport away and charm monster to make her way
through. The altar is chaotic!!! "I wonder if demigoddesses can have
harems?"

There is an altar to Anhur (chaotic) here.



