The next clan re-union was not the unalloyed triumph Angelika had
hoped for. It seems that the chubby Angelika was still annoyed about
having to do without her RoSD for a while ("I practically starved!"
she said unconvincingly -- Angelika guessed chubby had gained 20
pounds since she'd been gone), and had leaked some of the juicier
details of the ascension from the Wizard sub-clan's divination. Some
of the Angelikas didn't care, but most were wildly amused at
Angelika's extra-curricular antics. "Well, it got me the HP I needed
to survive didn't it?" True enough, but the knowing looks didn't
stop. Some non-chaotic Angelikas tried to explain that nurses were 
just supposed to HEAL you, not provide "extra services," but Angelika 
said they seemed to enjoy it, too. 

And then there was her cousin Angelika the Valkyrie. "*I* didn't die
during my ascension, and I had less than a third of your HP. I didn't
do any -- what was the euphemism you used?  Oh, right -- dancing. Oh,
and what about all *your* blunders, Ms. Super Smart!. Super Tart is
more like it!"

Angelika didn't care. Not much anyway. She was immortal and she had
brought an ascension to her sub-clan, only the second Angelika to do
that. She did wonder about the blunders, though. It was almost as if
there were some higher power, something beyond Anhur, beyond even Lord
Rng, a power that controlled all the Angelikas and caused them to act
similarly in spite of their differences. Angelika shrugged. Time
enough for philosophy later.

Angelika to lawful human Archeologist was shocked by Angelika's
actions. But, not by the "dancing." By the rampant destruction of
potentially valuable and scientifically interesting works of art. She
was also intrigued by the other reports she'd heard about the Dungeons
of Doom. A Castle! A Fort! What sights there were to be seen and
studied! She vowed she too would follow in the footsteps of her fellow
clan members -- but with a more studied eye.

